                                                              },
                                         "sendBody":  true,
                                         "specifyBody":  "json",
                                         "jsonBody":  "={{ JSON.stringify({ model: ({\"claude-haiku-latest\":\"claude-haiku-5-5\",\"claude-sonnet-latest\":\"claude-sonnet-5-5\",\"claude-opus-latest\":\"claude-opus-5-5\"}[$(\u0027Load model config\u0027).first().json.model.cv_extract] || null), max_tokens: 16000, system: \"You extract a structured career profile from a photographed or scanned CV / resume / Lebenslauf. Output ONLY a JSON object, no prose. All fields are optional - omit any field that is not clearly printed or readable; never invent. Output RAW printed values only - never compute or estimate. Fields: current_title = the current or most recent job title (string); industry = the sector of the current or most recent role (string); career_start_date = the start of the EARLIEST professional role listed, read off as printed (never add up durations; the database derives time spans); skills = array of objects {name, level one of beginner|intermediate|advanced|expert only if the document grades it else omit level, since = the year the skill was first used only if printed} - only clearly evidenced skills, at most 20; last_job_change_date = the start date of the current or most recent role. Dates keep the precision printed: a full German date DD.MM.YYYY becomes YYYY-MM-DD, a month-year like 03/2021 becomes 2021-03, a bare year stays 2014. Several files may come together, labelled File 1 of N and so on: read the pages of one CV together. If one of several files is not part of the CV, list its number in ignored_files (array of numbers). If the document is not a CV or resume, return {}.\", messages: [{ role: \u0027user\u0027, content: ($(\u0027Fetch telegram file\u0027).all().flatMap((x, n, all) =\u003e (all.length \u003e 1 ? [{ type: \u0027text\u0027, text: \u0027File \u0027 + (n + 1) + \u0027 of \u0027 + all.length + \u0027:\u0027 }] : []).concat([x.json.mime === \u0027application/pdf\u0027 ? { type: \u0027document\u0027, source: { type: \u0027base64\u0027, media_type: \u0027application/pdf\u0027, data: x.json.b64 } } : { type: \u0027image\u0027, source: { type: \u0027base64\u0027, media_type: x.json.mime, data: x.json.b64 } }])).concat([{ type: \u0027text\u0027, text: \u0027Document context from the user: \u0027 + ($(\u0027Start\u0027).item.json.doc_hint || \u0027none\u0027) + \u0027. Extract the career profile now.\u0027 }])) }], output_config: { effort: \u0027low\u0027 } }) }}",
